    "created_at": "2023-03-23T08:26:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-23T08:26:55Z",
    "body": "This actually protects against a use-after-free attack where the buffer is transferred away in the middle of being decompressed. Calling enqueue can result in executing user JavaScript. Maybe there should be a note about that.\r\n\r\nIt also ensures consistent and robust behaviour if JavaScript attempts to modify the buffer in the middle of decompression.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
